<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      LatSOF default-input selection — boot-time one-shot.

      Runs the latsof-default-input tool ONCE at each login. The tool
      waits up to 30 s for the LatSOF input device to appear (LatSOF
      publishes its engine ~1.5 s after kext start because initDSP
      defers off the matching thread, and a RunAtLoad agent can fire
      before that), sets it as the system default input, and exits.

      This fixes the boot race where AppleHDA's ghost "Internal
      Microphone" engine (published by AppleALC from a codec pin with
      no real mic behind it) wins the default-input heuristic because
      it registers first.

      Why a LaunchAgent (user) and not a LaunchDaemon (system):
        CoreAudio's default-input preference is a per-user HAL setting.
        A system daemon can enumerate devices but cannot set the user's
        default input reliably. This agent runs in the user GUI session.

      Why NO KeepAlive:
        Deliberate. The tool runs once per login and then gets out of
        the way — if you switch to a USB headset mid-session, macOS
        keeps your choice. (The old watch/KeepAlive mode re-asserted
        LatSOF every 10 s and would fight you; it is still available
        for debugging by running the tool with its watch flag.)

      Mic VOLUME is not handled here at all: the kext reads its own
      gain from NVRAM at engine init — `sudo nvram latsof.micvol=0.65`.

      Stop / uninstall:
        make uninstall    (from the source dir)
        or:
        launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.latsof.default-input.plist
        rm               ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.latsof.default-input.plist
    -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>local.latsof.default-input</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>@BINDIR@/latsof-default-input</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Run in the user GUI session so CoreAudio HAL calls land in the
         right per-user context. -->
    <key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key>
    <string>Aqua</string>

    <!-- Short-lived one-shot; never in the UI. -->
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <!-- Log to unified logging; view with:
         log show (predicate: processImagePath contains "latsof-default-input") -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/latsof-default-input.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/latsof-default-input.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
